{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":2621799,"ns":0,"title":"Condensed detachment","extract":"Condensed detachment (Rule D) is a method of finding the most general possible conclusion given two formal logical statements.\nIt was developed by the Irish logician Carew Meredith in the 1950s and inspired by the work of Łukasiewicz.","description":"Method in formal logic","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}